    "_postman_id": "8d1e7c28-9f24-4ac6-8d43-3ab1d2a80d01",
    "name": "Discord DMs Service - Gateway + Socket.IO",
    "description": "Postman collection for Team 17 Discord DMs Service, updated for Lab 2.\n\nREST:\n- Every client REST request goes through the API Gateway at http://localhost:8090.\n- Bearer JWTs are obtained through Player Service via the Gateway.\n- Existing intentional error tests are preserved.\n\nWebSocket / Socket.IO:\n- The client first negotiates through GET /ws/discord-dms on the Gateway.\n- The Gateway validates the JWT and returns the public Discord DMs URL.\n- The client then connects directly to Discord DMs, so the Gateway is not in the persistent socket path.\n\nIMPORTANT:\nThis file uses the legacy Postman Collection v2.1 JSON format, which represents HTTP requests. Postman's Socket.IO request type is stored separately from normal HTTP v2.1 collection requests. The collection therefore contains the complete HTTP setup/negotiation flow plus a self-contained channel preparation step. After running the Socket.IO Preparation folder, create two Socket.IO requests in Postman using the saved socketio_url and the event payloads documented in that folder.\n\nRun order:\n0. Setup - creates/logs in moderator and junior through Gateway.\n1. Gateway WebSocket Negotiation - tests 401 errors and successful negotiation.\n2. Channels / 3. Messages - existing REST tests.\n4. Socket.IO Preparation - creates a channel containing both test players.\n5. Gateway authorization checks - intentional 401 errors.\n\nSocket.IO events:\nModerator join_channel:\n{ \"channel_id\": \"{{socket_channel_id}}\", \"player_id\": \"{{player_id}}\" }\n\nJunior join_channel:\n{ \"channel_id\": \"{{socket_channel_id}}\", \"player_id\": \"{{junior_player_id}}\" }\n\nModerator send_message:\n{ \"channel_id\": \"{{socket_channel_id}}\", \"sender_id\": \"{{player_id}}\", \"content\": \"Hello from moderator through Socket.IO\" }\n\nListen for server event: message\n",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
