    {
      "name": "4. Socket.IO Preparation",
      "description": "Run these requests after Setup and Negotiation.\n\nThe first request creates a dedicated channel containing BOTH generated test players and saves socket_channel_id.\n\nThen in Postman create TWO Socket.IO requests:\n\nModerator Socket\nURL: {{socketio_url}}\nEmit join_channel:\n{\n  \"channel_id\": \"{{socket_channel_id}}\",\n  \"player_id\": \"{{player_id}}\"\n}\n\nJunior Socket\nURL: {{socketio_url}}\nEmit join_channel:\n{\n  \"channel_id\": \"{{socket_channel_id}}\",\n  \"player_id\": \"{{junior_player_id}}\"\n}\n\nOn Junior Socket, listen for event: message\n\nThen on Moderator Socket emit send_message:\n{\n  \"channel_id\": \"{{socket_channel_id}}\",\n  \"sender_id\": \"{{player_id}}\",\n  \"content\": \"Hello from moderator through Socket.IO\"\n}\n\nExpected: Junior receives the server event 'message' with the persisted message object.\n",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Create two-player Socket.IO test channel through Gateway",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('socket_session_id', pm.variables.replaceIn('{{$guid}}'));"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('socket_channel_id', body.id);",
                  "pm.test('Both players belong to channel', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.player_ids).to.include(pm.collectionVariables.get('player_id'));",
                  "  pm.expect(body.player_ids).to.include(pm.collectionVariables.get('junior_player_id'));",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"session_id\": \"{{socket_session_id}}\",\n  \"name\": \"socketio-test\",\n  \"player_ids\": [\n    \"{{player_id}}\",\n    \"{{junior_player_id}}\"\n  ]\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/channels",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "channels"
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Verify Socket.IO test channel through Gateway",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Correct socket channel returned', () => pm.expect(body.id).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('socket_channel_id')));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/channels/{{socket_channel_id}}",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "channels",
                "{{socket_channel_id}}"
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
